Short:        SMB2/3, AFP and NFS client, SMB file server
Author:       The Lagoon authors
Uploader:     The Lagoon authors
Type:         disk/misc
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     68020+, a TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library)
Distribution: Aminet

Lagoon mounts network shares as AmigaDOS volumes:

  * SMB 2.0.2 to 3.1.1 (signing, encryption): Windows, macOS file
    sharing, Samba and practically every NAS box
  * AFP 3.x over DSI: older Macs, AFP-only Time Capsules, Netatalk
  * NFS v3 over TCP: Linux, BSD and other Unix servers

and it shares the Amiga's own folders with Windows, macOS and Linux:
an SMB 2.0.2 to 3.1.1 server (NTLMv2 logons, signing, guest or password
shares, share lists, NetBIOS and mDNS so the Amiga is found by name).

It works over any bsdsocket.library stack (Riptide, Roadshow, Miami,
AmiTCP, Genesis). LagoonPrefs (GadTools, no MUI needed) edits the share
list, finds servers on the network (mDNS/Bonjour and NetBIOS), lists their
shares and tests the connection; its Sharing window shares folders. The Installer script sets everything up,
including mounting the shares at boot.

